  "problem": "Find $(A+B)-C-(B-C)$, if\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)-C-(B-C) & =A+B-C-B+C \\\\  & =A+\\cancel{B}-\\cancel{C}-\\cancel{B}+\\cancel{C} \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single matrix. So, the result is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
